<title>SOUTH KOREA: Shinhung Co says buying back shares.</title>
<headline>Shinhung Co says buying back shares.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shinhung Co Ltd said on Monday it will buy back 50,000 shares of its own common stock on the open market to boost share prices.  </p>
<p>The buyback, representing 3.75 percent of its share capital, will take place between January 24 and April 23, a company statement said.</p>
<p>Shinhung currently holds 80,147 of its own common shares, or 6.0 percent of its share capital.</p>
<p>The statement said the purchases would be made at the closing price of the previous day.</p>
<p>Shares of Shinhung rose 1,700 won on Monday to 24,000.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5645</p>
